# Zot safety

## Gate

Load on every Zot turn. Skip only when the turn never touches Zot
repositories, tags, GC, or auth.

## Read-only default

List repos and tags are fine when Zot work is authorized. Do **not**:

- delete a tag, manifest, or repository
- run GC that removes unreferenced blobs the user did not ask to prune
- change auth / anonymous pull policy without an explicit verb

…unless the user gave an **explicit verb this turn naming the object**.

## Mutate gates

| Action | Require |
| --- | --- |
| Delete tag | delete / remove + repository + tag |
| Delete repository | delete / remove / destroy + repository |
| GC / blob prune | gc / prune / garbage-collect + scope confirmation |
| Auth / anonymous pull | explicit auth/anonymous/public verb + intended policy |

Prefer the narrowest action:

1. Tag delete over repository wipe
2. Scoped GC after tag deletes over blind full GC
3. Ask once when mass-delete or GC scope is ambiguous

## Refuse secrets

Do **not** paste into chat:

- htpasswd entries, bearer tokens, or client certs
- Registry credentials or long-lived pull secrets

Prefer: repository/tag **names**, digest prefixes, and "credential is set"
language.

## No invented MCP tools

No Zot MCP was discovered in the live harness catalog. Do not invent MCP
tool names for delete/GC. Use API/UI/CLI paths the operator authorized.
If an MCP appears later, use only tools on the live map and still apply
these gates.

## Operator receipt (mutate)

Safe shape:

- Base URL product host (no credentials)
- Repository (+ tag when relevant)
- Action taken
- "No registry credentials shown"

